<title>JAPAN: Japan's OECF provides big loan to Thailand.</title>
<headline>Japan's OECF provides big loan to Thailand.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Overseas Economic Cooperation Fund (OECF) said on Friday it had signed a contract to provide 118.38 billion yen in loans to Thailand, its largest yen loan to the country.</p>
<p>The OECF, a government agency that provides concessionary financing for long-term development, said in a statement that the funds will be used for the construction of Thailand's subway system and seven other projects.</p>
<p>The cumulative total of OECF loan commitments to Thailand now stands at 1.38 trillion yen, it said.</p>
</text>
